  "question": {
    "text": "A monochromatic light is incident on a hydrogen sample in ground state. Hydrogen atoms absorb a fraction of light and subsequently emit radiation of six different wavelengths. The frequency of incident light is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>15</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math>. The value of x is ________<br />(Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>eVs</mi></math>)"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let the higher state be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>.</p><p>The number of wavelengths emitted is given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p>For hydrogen atom,<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mi>&#957;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>13</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>15</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mi>eV</mi></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#8658;</mo><mi>&#957;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>E</mi><mi>h</mi></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>13</mn><mo>.6</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>19</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>62</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>34</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>15</mn></msup><mi>Hz</mi></math></p>"
  }
}